WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.083
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:15.576
Unit five: Advanced Reported Speech. Today you will choose reporting verbs that show attitude and meaning.

4
00:00:15.876 --> 00:00:18.413
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.321
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:24.010
Claimed.

7
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:27.515
Claimed means said something without proving it.

8
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:29.768
He claimed he was innocent.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.571
Your turn. Say: Claimed.

10
00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:36.434
Claimed.

11
00:00:37.183 --> 00:00:38.208
Insisted.

12
00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:42.609
Insisted means said firmly, refusing to change.

13
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:44.926
She insisted on paying.

14
00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:48.111
Your turn. Say: Insisted.

15
00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.084
Insisted.

16
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:53.665
Denied.

17
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.963
Denied means said something is not true.

18
00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:58.853
They denied the rumour.

19
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.557
Your turn. Say: Denied.

20
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.389
Denied.

21
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.360
Reporting verb.

22
00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.743
Reporting verb means a verb that introduces reported words.

23
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.291
Admit is a reporting verb.

24
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:17.954
Your turn. Say: Reporting verb.

25
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.265
Reporting verb.

26
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:23.983
Nuance.

27
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:27.238
Nuance means a small difference in meaning.

28
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.559
A nuance of attitude.

29
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.651
Your turn. Say: Nuance.

30
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.652
Nuance.

31
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:38.662
Implication.

32
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.184
Implication means a meaning that is suggested.

33
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:44.481
The implication was clear.

34
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:47.457
Your turn. Say: Implication.

35
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.382
Implication.

36
00:01:52.117 --> 00:01:53.211
Indirect meaning.

37
00:01:54.217 --> 00:01:57.099
Indirect meaning means meaning not said directly.

38
00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.253
Look for indirect meaning.

39
00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.885
Your turn. Say: Indirect meaning.

40
00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:06.967
Indirect meaning.

41
00:02:07.717 --> 00:02:08.416
Tone.

42
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:11.811
Tone means the attitude shown by words.

43
00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:13.963
A sceptical tone.

44
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.564
Your turn. Say: Tone.

45
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.134
Tone.

46
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:24.665
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.517 --> 00:02:28.596
Visal, why do reporters write claimed instead of said?

48
00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:40.047
Said is neutral. Claimed suggests the speaker has not proved it, and insisted shows determination. The reporting verb adds the writer's view of the statement.

49
00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.184
What patterns follow these verbs?

50
00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:57.274
Some take that-clauses: She claimed that she had won. Some take gerunds: He admitted taking the money. Others take to-infinitives: They promised to help. Denied takes a gerund or a that-clause.

51
00:02:58.383 --> 00:03:00.383
Do we always change the tense?

52
00:03:01.483 --> 00:03:12.681
We backshift when the report is past: She said she was tired. But if the statement is still true, we can keep the present: She said the museum opens at nine.

53
00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:15.670
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.517 --> 00:03:23.253
Grammar focus: Reported speech: subject plus reporting verb plus that-clause and gerund and infinitive.

55
00:03:23.553 --> 00:03:24.798
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.483 --> 00:03:27.692
He insisted that he had paid already.

57
00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:30.304
She denied taking the money.

58
00:03:31.217 --> 00:03:33.483
They promised to finish the work on time.

59
00:03:34.433 --> 00:03:41.521
Choose the reporting verb for its meaning and its pattern: claim, insist, deny, admit, promise. Backshift only when needed.

60
00:03:42.283 --> 00:03:45.923
Be careful! Don't say: He denied to take it.

61
00:03:47.867 --> 00:03:49.843
Say: He denied taking it.

62
00:03:50.143 --> 00:03:51.550
Deny takes a gerund.

63
00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.764
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.113
What Did He Really Say?.

65
00:03:57.413 --> 00:04:00.110
The manager claimed that the project was on schedule.

66
00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.680
The workers insisted that they had not been told.

67
00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.980
He denied making any promise to the staff.

68
00:04:07.967 --> 00:04:10.523
Each reporting verb shows a different attitude.

69
00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:14.276
The words people use can change the story.

70
00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:19.148
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:19.983 --> 00:04:21.565
He blank that he had paid.

72
00:04:21.865 --> 00:04:25.785
A, insisted. B, insist. C, insisting.

73
00:04:29.333 --> 00:04:31.704
The answer is A: insisted.

74
00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.571
She denied blank the money.

75
00:04:34.871 --> 00:04:38.130
A, to take. B, taking. C, take.

76
00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.330
The answer is B: taking.

77
00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:47.400
Which verb suggests the speaker has not proved it?

78
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.377
A, claimed. B, said. C, asked.

79
00:04:54.933 --> 00:04:56.770
The answer is A: claimed.

80
00:04:57.917 --> 00:04:59.475
They promised blank help.

81
00:04:59.775 --> 00:05:02.987
A, to. B, helping. C, that.

82
00:05:06.533 --> 00:05:08.196
The answer is A: to.

83
00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.232
According to the reading, what did the workers insist?

84
00:05:12.532 --> 00:05:16.859
A, they had not been told. B, they were paid. C, they were late.

85
00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.224
The answer is A: they had not been told.

86
00:05:24.433 --> 00:05:27.422
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:28.283 --> 00:05:31.363
Report a statement using 'insisted' instead of 'said'.

88
00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.662
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.962 --> 00:05:54.718
He said, 'I paid yesterday.' This becomes: He insisted that he had paid the day before. I chose insisted because it shows he was firm and did not want to change his answer.

90
00:05:55.018 --> 00:05:56.727
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:57.617 --> 00:06:05.377
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported speech: subject plus reporting verb plus that-clause and gerund and infinitive.

92
00:06:05.677 --> 00:06:09.793
Today's value is truthfulness. Tell the truth and check the facts.

93
00:06:10.093 --> 00:06:12.675
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:12.975 --> 00:06:15.755
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

